# Shorten explicit directed pairs of base-to-robot tether configurations on
# the cached map. Every non-empty input Path must use the map frame, be
# oriented from one exactly identical tether base to its robot endpoint, and
# be a complete collision-free, locally shortest (taut), piecewise-linear
# topology reference. Every reference is traced and shortened in full before
# exact common prefixes are removed for pairwise shortening. When a
# configuration comes from PathResult, pass
# topology_path rather than the densely sampled path.
# Result paths run from the source robot pose to the destination robot pose
# and may cross CDT triangle interiors.
unique_identifier_msgs/UUID map_id
# Optional compatibility guard. Zero lets Raystar derive the environment from
# map_id and allow_unknown; non-zero requires an exact match before UPS work.
unique_identifier_msgs/UUID expected_environment_id
# Aggregate admission is controlled by max_transition_configurations and
# max_path_points, independently of multi-goal/path-enumeration limits.
nav_msgs/Path[] tether_configurations
# Pairs are directed, retain request order, and index tether_configurations.
# Aggregate admission is controlled by max_transition_pairs.
raystar_interfaces/ConfigurationTransitionPair[] transition_pairs
bool allow_unknown
---
# success is true only after every requested pair has been processed and every
# returned transition is certified. A geometric/certification failure still
# produces its ordered per-pair record, but makes the aggregate status FAILED.
uint8 STATUS_UNKNOWN=0
uint8 STATUS_COMPLETE=1
uint8 STATUS_INVALID_REQUEST=2
uint8 STATUS_CANCELLED=3
uint8 STATUS_FAILED=4
# Cooperative planning_timeout_ms expiration. This is distinct from an
# accepted client cancellation and normally terminates the Action as aborted.
uint8 STATUS_TIMEOUT=5
bool success
# Echoes the identity used for the request, including failure results.
unique_identifier_msgs/UUID map_id
# Actual content/policy/semantic environment used, including failure results
# once the cached map and startup configuration have been resolved.
unique_identifier_msgs/UUID environment_id
uint8 status
# requested_transition_count is the admitted goal's pair-array size.
# completed_transition_count is the number of ordered per-pair records that
# were fully evaluated and appended; it is not the number that succeeded.
uint32 requested_transition_count
uint32 completed_transition_count
string message
raystar_interfaces/HomotopyTransitionResult[] transitions
---
# Counts are monotonic and stage is diagnostic text, not a machine state enum.
# The producer emits validation/environment/pair stages, including the first
# and last pair progress, with at most 100 feedback messages total. Action
# feedback is a volatile, non-authoritative live stream, not a complete event
# log: a client may miss an ordered prefix or intermediate samples. Result is
# authoritative.
uint32 requested_transition_count
uint32 completed_transition_count
string stage
